<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Afrox year earnings up 18 percent.</title>
<headline>Afrox year earnings up 18 percent.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended September 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Shr (cts)</p>
<p>    - historic cost	 66.0	  vs 56.0</p>
<p>    - current cost	  60.0	  vs 51.0</p>
<p>    Div cts)		  32.0	  vs 27.7</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   181.45	vs 152.85</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   294.11	vs 249.09</p>
<p>    Tax			 104.62	vs 90.92</p>
<p>    Historic oper profit  381.77	vs 328.70</p>
<p>    Add depreciation	18.04	 vs 15.52</p>
<p>    Current oper profit   363.74	vs 313.18</p>
<p>    Net interest paid     69.63	 vs 64.09</p>
<p>    Turnover		  2,009.71    vs 1,723.24</p>
<p>Div payable January 29</p>
<p>on register November 22</p>
<p>Full name: African Oxygen Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said it was offering capitalisation shares in lieu of the final dividend of 20.5 cents.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
